1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,098
Lesson 3.3.5: Gaps in Care and Complications.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:13,775
This lesson covers the next three sections of the problem note.

3
00:00:13,825 --> 00:00:17,892
Gaps in care are the monitoring or treatment the condition is missing,

4
00:00:17,932 --> 00:00:21,452
and the Care Gaps tab lists them for each condition.

5
00:00:21,502 --> 00:00:25,293
Risk factors and complications come from the Conditions Guide,

6
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:28,673
and each one is checked against the patient's record.

7
00:00:28,723 --> 00:00:30,713
And symptoms come from the same guide;

8
00:00:30,753 --> 00:00:34,307
the progress notes tell us whether the patient has any.

9
00:00:35,567 --> 00:00:39,553
Before we go on, there's an easier way to build the note than a sticky note:

10
00:00:39,593 --> 00:00:44,145
the Problem Note Generator in the CCM Clinical Tool.

11
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:49,790
We type the condition, hyperlipidemia,

12
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:55,080
and pick its ICD-10 code exactly as PointClickCare lists it.

13
00:00:58,333 --> 00:01:00,288
The template adjusts to the condition,

14
00:01:00,328 --> 00:01:04,361
and everything we fill in appears in the live note below.

15
00:01:06,533 --> 00:01:08,283
The medication, for example,

16
00:01:08,323 --> 00:01:11,846
goes in its own field and lands in the note right away.

17
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:19,043
Medication adherence has a dropdown that covers every scenario:

18
00:01:19,083 --> 00:01:24,552
refusals, missed days, PRN never given, X, or blank days.

19
00:01:27,233 --> 00:01:30,640
For our patient, it's simple: the patient is adherent.

20
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,923
Lifestyle modifications work the same way:

21
00:01:34,964 --> 00:01:38,031
the diet, the adherence, and any therapy.

22
00:01:38,081 --> 00:01:40,773
We'll keep filling in the note with it as we go.

23
00:01:44,733 --> 00:01:49,943
Next comes gaps in care: the monitoring or treatment this condition is missing.

24
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,874
The Update Care Policy has a tab just for them,

25
00:01:53,914 --> 00:01:57,152
Care Gaps, listing the gaps for each condition.

26
00:01:58,233 --> 00:02:00,665
For hyperlipidemia, there are four.

27
00:02:00,715 --> 00:02:05,817
The lipid panel, either not monitored recently or uncontrolled if recent.

28
00:02:05,867 --> 00:02:08,911
And three for blood pressure: not monitored recently,

29
00:02:08,951 --> 00:02:13,649
not monitored regularly, or uncontrolled over the last 10 days.

30
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:16,438
We check each one against the patient's record.

31
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:25,965
The Numbers To Track tab says the lipid profile is due every 180 days,

32
00:02:26,005 --> 00:02:27,283
about six months.

33
00:02:32,133 --> 00:02:36,594
In the Results tab, the last lipid panel was collected on July 15,

34
00:02:36,634 --> 00:02:40,767
2026: still within those six months.

35
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,683
And every value was in range: total cholesterol, triglycerides, HDL and LDL.

36
00:02:54,467 --> 00:02:57,025
So the lipid panel is monitored and controlled,

37
00:02:57,065 --> 00:02:59,404
and this first gap doesn't apply.

38
00:03:00,267 --> 00:03:04,965
The other three gaps are all about blood pressure, which is monitored every day.

39
00:03:06,067 --> 00:03:10,169
So we open the patient's blood pressure readings in Weights and Vitals.

40
00:03:10,233 --> 00:03:14,248
The last reading was on November 12: 13 days before today,

41
00:03:14,288 --> 00:03:18,697
the 25th. So blood pressure isn't monitored recently.

42
00:03:18,747 --> 00:03:22,916
Monitored regularly means a reading every day for the past 10 days.

43
00:03:22,956 --> 00:03:26,867
There's none at all, so it isn't monitored regularly either.

44
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,296
And readings at or above 140 over 90,

45
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:36,149
like 148 over 68, mean it isn't controlled.

46
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:43,964
Back in the generator, ticking a gap adds it to the note.

47
00:03:46,133 --> 00:03:51,102
Still, writing the gaps in our own words keeps the note clear and easy to read.

48
00:03:51,233 --> 00:03:54,691
So the note reads: BP wasn't monitored recently,

49
00:03:54,731 --> 00:03:59,977
BP is not monitored regularly, and BP is not controlled.

50
00:04:00,933 --> 00:04:05,017
In short: we take the condition's possible gaps from the care policy,

51
00:04:05,057 --> 00:04:09,866
check each one against the patient, and document every gap that applies.

52
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:17,525
The next section is the presence of risk factors

53
00:04:17,565 --> 00:04:22,050
and complications due to uncontrolled hyperlipidemia.

54
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:25,789
The Conditions Guide tab lists both for each condition.

55
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:32,782
For hyperlipidemia, the risk factors are a diet high in saturated fats or sugar,

56
00:04:32,822 --> 00:04:40,040
being overweight or obese, not enough exercise, smoking, and uncontrolled comorbidities.

57
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:44,569
Each one has its own place to check: the progress notes for diet and smoking,

58
00:04:44,609 --> 00:04:50,873
the BMI for weight, therapy for exercise, and the labs for comorbidities.

59
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:59,369
Diet first: a keyword search of the progress notes,

60
00:04:59,409 --> 00:05:03,854
for saturated fats and then for sugar, finds nothing relevant.

61
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:11,038
Weight comes from Weights and Vitals: the latest weight is 191.7 pounds.

62
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:18,118
And the weight summary shows a BMI of 25.3.

63
00:05:18,168 --> 00:05:22,510
A BMI from 25 to 29.9 counts as overweight,

64
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:27,185
so the patient is slightly overweight: that's our first risk factor.

65
00:05:31,667 --> 00:05:35,315
For exercise, the Care Profile's Therapies section is empty:

66
00:05:35,355 --> 00:05:38,586
no physical or occupational therapy.

67
00:05:38,636 --> 00:05:42,593
That counts as physical inactivity, our second risk factor.

68
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:50,745
Both go into the note: the patient is slightly overweight,

69
00:05:50,785 --> 00:05:52,877
with physical inactivity.

70
00:05:52,933 --> 00:05:57,881
For smoking, a progress note search for smoking and for cigarettes finds nothing,

71
00:05:57,921 --> 00:06:00,590
so the patient isn't an active smoker.

72
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:06,421
So our patient has two risk factors:

73
00:06:06,461 --> 00:06:10,122
being slightly overweight, and physical inactivity.

74
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:15,614
Complications come from the same column of the Conditions Guide.

75
00:06:16,567 --> 00:06:20,895
Atherosclerosis, heart, brain and blood vessel complications,

76
00:06:20,935 --> 00:06:26,220
hepatic steatosis, xanthomas and xanthelasma, and pancreatitis.

77
00:06:26,270 --> 00:06:28,087
These are all medical conditions,

78
00:06:28,127 --> 00:06:31,837
so the patient's diagnoses tell us which ones apply.

79
00:06:34,033 --> 00:06:38,359
In the Med Diag tab, we read through every active diagnosis.

80
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:46,733
None of them is on the list, so the note says: no documented complications.

81
00:06:48,367 --> 00:06:52,367
Any complication we did find would be listed here by name.

82
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,960
The last section here is symptoms.

83
00:07:00,167 --> 00:07:04,363
The Conditions Guide lists the possible symptoms of hyperlipidemia:

84
00:07:04,403 --> 00:07:08,938
chest pain, abdominal pain, and fatty tissue deposits.

85
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:13,131
A progress note search for each of them finds nothing.

86
00:07:17,433 --> 00:07:20,007
So the patient is marked asymptomatic.

87
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:29,292
And every section we update appears straight away in the problem note below.

88
00:07:36,533 --> 00:07:41,347
To wrap up: the Problem Note Generator builds the note section by section.

89
00:07:41,397 --> 00:07:43,620
Gaps in care come from the Care Gaps tab,

90
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:47,078
and each one is checked against the patient's record.

91
00:07:47,128 --> 00:07:49,467
Risk factors come from the Conditions Guide:

92
00:07:49,507 --> 00:07:53,984
diet, weight, exercise, smoking and comorbidities.

93
00:07:54,034 --> 00:07:58,424
Complications are checked against the patient's active diagnoses.

94
00:07:58,474 --> 00:08:00,925
And symptoms come from a progress note search.

95
00:08:00,965 --> 00:08:04,111
With none, the patient is asymptomatic.

96
00:08:06,267 --> 00:08:09,468
Next, we document falls and provider visits.
